{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/576040-willpower-change-or-typo","id":576040,"title":"Willpower Change or Typo","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-07-01T22:32:25-07:00","id":576040,"title":"Willpower Change or Typo","content":"I feel bad bringing this up so late, but it caused a pretty sour rules argument in one of my groups and I wanted to figure out what was what!<br /> <br /> p159 of the 2E core says &quot;You can only spend one point of Willpower per action.&quot;<br /> <br /> The core blue book says on p95 &quot;Only one Willpower point can be spent per turn to achieve any one of the following effects.&quot;<br /> <br /> Really only noticed this because we have a guy new to the NWOD who got mad when he wasn't allowed to spend 1WP on his attack and 1WP to boost def like he thought he could. Was this a stealthy rules change I missed in 2E or a lingering typo because everyone skimmed past this section?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1134-nicias","name":"Nicias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"274"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-01T22:41:54-07:00","id":576066,"title":"","content":"Pretty sure it's a typo.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-02T02:42:39-07:00","id":576248,"title":"","content":"I always read that as meaning precisely what it was supposed to. I think if it meant you could activate all of the effects once there would be an &quot;each&quot; in there somewhere.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-02T07:04:30-07:00","id":576316,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/576040-willpower-change-or-typo#post576040\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I feel bad bringing this up so late, but it caused a pretty sour rules argument in one of my groups and I wanted to figure out what was what!<br /> <br /> p159 of the 2E core says &quot;You can only spend one point of Willpower per action.&quot;<br /> <br /> The core blue book says on p95 &quot;Only one Willpower point can be spent per turn to achieve any one of the following effects.&quot;<br /> <br /> Really only noticed this because we have a guy new to the NWOD who got mad when he wasn't allowed to spend 1WP on his attack and 1WP to boost def like he thought he could. Was this a stealthy rules change I missed in 2E or a lingering typo because everyone skimmed past this section?</div> </div> </div> </div>Pretty sure the original intent for the core blue book was still only one Willpower point per turn (which you can get a single one of the following effects for spending).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-02T07:26:50-07:00","id":576335,"title":"","content":"I think the OP is saying that the confusion is about the WtF 2e core, which says once per <i>action</i> instead of once per <i>turn</i>, which the player took to mean he could use one Willpower to bolster his action and one to resist his opponent's action in the same turn, since they're separate actions. I'm 99.9% sure that is not how it's intended to work.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-02T19:00:05-07:00","id":576972,"title":"","content":"Yeah, that was the player's read and one that I couldn't easily refute with anything other then &quot;we're gonna handle it this way,&quot; which is perfectly serviceable but - suboptimal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1134-nicias","name":"Nicias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"274"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-03T06:15:00-07:00","id":577288,"title":"","content":"I'll just come in here and point out that since the rules are the same in WtF 2e and VtR 2e (including the typos...) this is corroborated by another rule book...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/585-seidmadr","name":"Seidmadr","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar585_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-03T22:43:32-07:00","id":578250,"title":"","content":"&quot;Turn&quot; and &quot;Action&quot; are almost synonymous in the system, and often used interchangeably. Instant Action is what can be done in one turn, separate from Reflexive Actions. The intention is 1 Willpower spent in one combat turn, either to activate a power or grant extra successes, but not both at the same time. This creates an economy of Willpower, in that powers that require Willpower to be spent to activate are written slightly more powerful in effect, because you can't also get +3 dice on the roll by spending Willpower, unless it's an Extended Roll over multiple turns.<br /> <br /> The rule was before a bunch of Reflexive powers were introduced, of course, but still would apply. Similar to having a limit to the amount of Essence that can be spent in a turn, really.<br /> <br /> So yes, the player read is technically correct, but the intention is a turn.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/137x125q90/745/a5GS5M.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/802-amaterasu","name":"amaterasu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"208"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-04T02:10:22-07:00","id":578464,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>amaterasu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/576040-willpower-change-or-typo?p=578250#post578250\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;Turn&quot; and &quot;Action&quot; are almost synonymous in the system, and often used interchangeably. Instant Action is what can be done in one turn, separate from Reflexive Actions. The intention is 1 Willpower spent in one combat turn, either to activate a power or grant extra successes, but not both at the same time. This creates an economy of Willpower, in that powers that require Willpower to be spent to activate are written slightly more powerful in effect, because you can't also get +3 dice on the roll by spending Willpower, unless it's an Extended Roll over multiple turns.<br /> <br /> The rule was before a bunch of Reflexive powers were introduced, of course, but still would apply. Similar to having a limit to the amount of Essence that can be spent in a turn, really.<br /> <br /> So yes, the player read is technically correct, but the intention is a turn.</div> </div> </div> </div>The mix-up happens when you put Extended Actions into the picture.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-04T20:16:21-07:00","id":579332,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/576040-willpower-change-or-typo?p=578464#post578464\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The mix-up happens when you put Extended Actions into the picture.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which is why it should have been written as per turn, but it's something that slipped by.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/137x125q90/745/a5GS5M.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/802-amaterasu","name":"amaterasu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"208"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-06T00:00:48-07:00","id":580591,"title":"","content":"That line is supposed to indicate you cannot spend multiple points of Willpower on any particular, specific action. It's still one Willpower per turn as long as we are using the GMC rules (which 2ed is using), that line should probably be updated in the pdf at some point to say you may spend one Willpower per turn instead of action.<br /> <br /> It seems to me the thinking was we get one action per turn so we could only spend one Willpower per turn and that line was meant to make that clear, forgetting that you can use it add 2 to Defense against a single opponent for one turn. If the sections were written by different people it's easy to picture how the slip probably occurred.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Onyx Path Forum Administrator</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><b><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">Posts in this color are moderator posts</span></b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\"><span style=\"color:#00FF00\">Posts in this color mean a Great Old One has driven me mad.</span></span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11-darksider","name":"Darksider","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11_2.jpeg","title":"Forum Administrator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1692"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-06T00:15:19-07:00","id":580596,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/576040-willpower-change-or-typo?p=578464#post578464\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The mix-up happens when you put Extended Actions into the picture.</div> </div> </div> </div>Make an attack, spend Willpower. Get attacked that same turn and spend Willpower to add 2 to Defense against one opponent for the turn. 2 separate chances to spend Willpower in the same turn. You don't need Extended actions to introduce the confusion.<br /> <br /> Thinking further on it, other than limiting the expenditure to one point per action, what real harm does letting a player burn through Willpower really do? You get it back fairly regularly and the game is meant to have you spending Willpower pretty frequently, so burning a bunch now may leave you short later when you need it. Just remember your opponents have Willpower to spend too.<br /> <br /> I say give it a try the way the player thought it was supposed to work, keeping in mind if you let a player do something then it's possible for non-mook NPC's as well. They were technically correct, the best kind of correct. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Onyx Path Forum Administrator</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><b><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">Posts in this color are moderator posts</span></b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\"><span style=\"color:#00FF00\">Posts in this color mean a Great Old One has driven me mad.</span></span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":11,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11-darksider","user":"Darksider","date":". 07-06-2015, 03:30 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11-darksider","name":"Darksider","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11_2.jpeg","title":"Forum Administrator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1692"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-06T23:06:50-07:00","id":581980,"title":"","content":"I can see an argument for that, but I prefer 1WP/turn as a way of creating choices and consequences for them. Especially when - maybe this is a group style thing - I'm used to seeing most fights end early enough that you could use 2WP for the majority of rounds if not all of them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1134-nicias","name":"Nicias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"274"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}